    "title": "Is Chime Down? Widespread outages as app access fails",
    "text": "Chime experienced a widespread outage, according to multiple tracking services and Chime’s own status page. Thousands of users across the United States reported problems Wednesday with logging in, accessing balances, sending money and using the mobile app, according to Downdetector data and third‑party outage monitors. By 4:30 p.m. ET, Chime reports were down to 143, according to Downdetector.Earlier Wednesday, Chime said that most complaints centered on the Chime app and website not loading or returning error messages, with some users saying they were unable to access their funds during the disruption.Is Chime Currently Down?Chime acknowledged the issue on its official status page, saying it was investigating a platform‑wide service disruption. \"Chime said on its status page, \"Card purchases and ATM transactions are working normally. The money in your account and your personal information are secure.\"A Chime logo is shown outside the company's office in San Francisco, Saturday, February 24, 2024. (AP Photo/Jeff Chiu)When Could Chime Service Resume?As of the latest update Wednesday, Chime said engineers were continuing to work to resolve the issue, while outage reports from users dropped throughout the afternoon.What is Chime?Chime is a financial technology company that provides app‑based banking services through partnerships with FDIC‑insured banks, primarily The Bancorp Bank and Stride Bank. While often referred to as a banking app, Chime itself is not a bank. It offers features similar to traditional checking and savings accounts, including direct deposit, debit cards, bill payments and mobile money transfers, all managed through a digital platform without physical branches.The company has grown rapidly by targeting customers seeking low‑fee, mobile‑first alternatives to traditional banking, including people who may have limited access to brick‑and‑mortar banks. Chime does not charge monthly maintenance fees and markets products such as early direct deposit and fee‑free overdraft coverage, though access to certain features depends on account activity. Funds held in Chime accounts are insured through its partner banks, up to standard federal limits.Updates: 4/1/26, 4:54 p.m. ET: This article was updated with new information.",
